n-scope serving-stack image (KServe components and serving data\n53\t  plane).\n54\t- No in-scope image links a non-validated cryptographic library in the\n55\t  request path.\n56\t- The serving stack serves inference requests correctly on a FIPS-enabled\n57\t  OpenShift cluster (end-to-end verification).\n58\t- All remediated images build green through their existing Konflux\n59\t  pipelines.\n60\t\n61\t## HLR Traceability\n62\t\n63\tHLR-1 — all serving-stack images run correctly on FIPS-enabled clusters using\n64\tvalidated crypto modules (KServe and serving data plane portion). The module\n65\tinventory produced here feeds HLR-2's evidence package.\n66\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a1b4f8e1156e58df","agent_id":"ae94751e2b2cffef3","session_id":"4a043728-3f47-48a2-8b4d-164c061f2c18","uuid":"5e5ea980-ec2c-4c12-9691-b402bfc33558","timestamp":"2026-10-22T01:39:17.038Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8ffc42ddd27347de","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9013 decomposition"}
